 ### [Single Scattering Illumination](9628-single-scattering-illumination.md)
-Single Scattering Illumination is a volumetric lighting model that computes the radiance contribution of light undergoing exactly one scattering event within a participating medium. It solves the problem of realistic volumetric lighting by distinguishing between light scattered along the view ray (Direct Single Scattering, DSS) and light scattered along illumination rays from scene points (Indirect Single Scattering, ISS). Unlike basic volume rendering which often ignores volumetric shadows or uses approximations, this method provides an analytic formulation for both direct and indirect contributions, including occlusion handling via shadow volumes, enabling real-time hardware rendering of complex volumetric lighting effects.
+Single Scattering Illumination is a volumetric lighting model that computes the radiance contribution of light undergoing exactly one scattering event within a participating medium. It distinguishes between light scattered along the view ray (Direct Single Scattering, DSS) and light scattered along illumination rays from scene points (Indirect Single Scattering, ISS). Unlike basic volume rendering that often ignores volumetric shadows, this method provides an analytic formulation for both contributions, including occlusion handling via shadow volumes, enabling real-time hardware rendering.
 
